      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1977 the resort‑style community sold out, later shifting from vacation homes to about 3,700 year‑round residences.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_Valley_Springs%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bear Valley Springs is a semi‑public gated community; its roads are funded solely by local property taxes, not county or state money.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_Valley_Springs%2C_California",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Former President Ronald Reagan once owned a ranch in Bear Valley Springs, adding a touch of presidential history to the valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_Valley_Springs%2C_California",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Bear Valley Springs Association, formed after the sale, manages the community’s amenities and preserves the original natural value of the land.",
